From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 10:26:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] HFR VRR: actions and infolabels for the 3D glasses delay and Invert

A skin can offer the 3D glasses delay and the eye swap where it offers
the audio and subtitle offsets (its stream select dialogs) rather than
only inside the player's video settings:

- Action fs3ddelay (273) opens the slider dialog for the 3D glasses
  delay, as audiodelay does for the audio offset, with the setting's own
  range and step. A change applies at once; it is a display setting, not
  the film's, saved with the others when Kodi exits (as the volume is),
  not on every step of the slider.
- Action stereoinvert (274) swaps the eyes of the playing video (its
  Invert stereoscopic 3D mode, saved with the film like the dialog's
  toggle) and says which way it now is.
- Player.Fs3dDelay shows the delay ("1300 µs") and the boolean
  Player.StereoInvert whether the eyes are swapped, for button labels.

Shared code: actions, infolabels and the player controller are generic
Kodi; nothing here is Amlogic-specific.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
